# Code ownership → required reviewers.
#
# The security gate must not be silently neutered in the same PR that introduces
# a threat: a change that plants a secret while adding a .gitleaks allowlist regex
# (or a self-authored waiver) should force a second reviewer on the gate's own
# config. These entries name that reviewer; they take effect once branch
# protection ("Require review from Code Owners") is enabled on the default branch
# in the repo settings — the file documents the control even before that toggle.

# The security tooling, its configs, and the waiver ledger.
/ops/security/**        @iamvaln
/.semgrep/**            @iamvaln
/.gitleaks.toml         @iamvaln
/security-waivers.yml   @iamvaln
/docs/security/**       @iamvaln

# The release gate + CI workflows (the deploy gate and the security job live here).
/.github/workflows/**   @iamvaln
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @iamvaln
